---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Katabarwa Labs"
  description="Katabarwa Labs privacy policy. Our applications run inside your own cloud or SaaS tenant; we operate no backend and do not collect, store, or transmit your operational data."
>
  <section class="bg-[linear-gradient(160deg,#0a1636,#152f6b)] text-[#eaf0ff]">
    <div class="wrap pt-[52px] pb-[46px]">
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(26px,4vw,36px)] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] text-[#a9bce6]">Katabarwa Labs Inc · Effective 7 August 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-6 pt-11 pb-[72px]">
    <div class="callout"><strong>The short version:</strong> our applications run <em>inside your own</em>
      cloud subscription, cloud account, or SaaS instance, under an identity you control. We operate no
      servers that receive your data. We do not collect, store, or transmit your operational data, logs,
      resource metadata, secrets, or content. Alerts and reports are sent only to the destination
      <em>you</em> configure — for example, your own Microsoft Teams, Slack, or email.</div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>Katabarwa Labs Inc (“Katabarwa Labs”, “we”, “us”) builds single-purpose operational tools
      distributed through enterprise marketplaces, including the Microsoft Azure Marketplace and
      Microsoft AppSource, the AWS Marketplace, and the Atlassian Marketplace.</p>

    <h2>2. How our applications handle your data</h2>
    <p>Our applications are deployed into your own environment (your Azure subscription, AWS account, or
      Atlassian/SaaS instance) and execute there using a managed identity, IAM role, or app permissions
      that you grant and can revoke. They read only the metadata required to perform their function,
      keep any state inside your environment, and send output only to the notification endpoint you
      configure. <strong>Your operational data never reaches Katabarwa Labs.</strong> Uninstalling or
      deleting the application removes it and its data from your environment.</p>

    <h2>3. Information we do receive</h2>
    <p>We receive a limited amount of information <em>from the marketplace</em> in order to transact and
      support you — not from your deployed application:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Purchase &amp; subscription data</strong> provided by the marketplace (e.g., company
        name, the fact of a subscription, and billing status). Payment card details are handled by the
        marketplace/cloud provider, not by us.</li>
      <li><strong>Support communications</strong> you send us directly (e.g., your email and the
        contents of a support request).</li>
      <li><strong>Basic website information</strong> if you visit this site (standard server request
        data). We do not use advertising trackers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How we use it</h2>
    <p>Only to (a) provide and support the products you have subscribed to, (b) meet legal, tax, and
      accounting obligations, and (c) communicate with you about your subscription. We do not sell your
      information, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

    <h2>5. Sharing</h2>
    <p>We share information only with the <strong>marketplace / cloud provider</strong> that bills and
      delivers the product (Microsoft, Amazon Web Services, or Atlassian), and service providers we use
      for accounting, tax, and payments — each only as needed. We may disclose information if required
      by law.</p>

    <h2>6. Retention</h2>
    <p>We keep the limited marketplace and support information above only as long as needed for the
      purposes described or as required by law, then delete it. Data inside your own environment is
      retained and deleted under your control.</p>

    <h2>7. Security</h2>
    <p>Because our applications run in your environment and we do not receive your operational data, the
      primary controls are the ones you already operate (your identity, IAM, and network controls). For
      the limited information we do hold, we apply reasonable administrative and technical safeguards.</p>

    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Subject to applicable law, you may request access to, correction of, or deletion of the personal
      information we hold about you. Email us and we will respond.</p>

    <h2>9. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy; the “Effective” date above reflects the latest version. Material
      changes will be reflected on this page.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>Katabarwa Labs Inc — <a class="text-brand" href="mailto:abaho@llmgraph.ai">email us</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
